Then the short-time Fourier transform $V_\varphi\sigma$ never vanishes:
\[
V_\varphi \sigma(x,\omega) \;\neq\; 0 \qquad \text{for all }\;(x,\omega)\in\rr{2}.
\]
Moreover, we have the strict lower bound
\begin{equation}\label{eq:lowerbound}
\bigl|V_\varphi \sigma(x,\omega)\bigr|
\;>\; \frac{1}{2\pi}\,e^{-\pi x^2}
\qquad \text{for all }\;(x,\omega)\in\rr{2}.
\end{equation}
